{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Wine and strong drink</b> — if he drank a quarter-log of wine he is forbidden to give instruction. תשת is notarikon תפל\"ת שכו\"ר תועב\"ה (you prayed, you became drunk, an abomination)." "<b>You and your sons</b> — in gematria: the invalidated priests and those with blemishes went out." "<b>Wine and strong drink</b> — no verse begins with 'wine' except this one, which brought wailing into the world, for they were drunk with wine and therefore died."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "Notarikon expansions translated word-for-word: תפל\"ת = תפלת (you prayed); שכו\"ר = שכור (drunk); תועב\"ה = תועבה (abomination).", 1 "The gematria equates אתה ובניך with יצאו החללים ובעלי מומין; the Hebrew equated phrase is translated but no numeric value is given by the author."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:10.496366854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}